{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Miriam spoke, and Aaron, about Moses.</b> How did she know that Moses had separated from his wife? She saw that Tziporah was not adorning herself with women's jewelry. She said to her: does your brother not mind this? Through this Miriam knew, and she told her brother, and both of them spoke about him." "<b>On account of the Cushite woman.</b> They said: why did he separate now from his wife? Was it because she is a Cushite? But he married a Cushite woman from the time of the marriage — she was dark from the time of the marriage, and he did not leave her because of her darkness, so why did he leave her now because of her darkness. Another interpretation: <b>on account of the Cushite woman</b> — a Cushite queen, as written in Divrei HaYamim about Moses, and he did not consort with her. And one should not explain this about Tziporah, for if so, what is the meaning of what is written, כי אשה כושית לקח — and did we not know until now that he took Tziporah? Furthermore, Tziporah was not a Cushite, for Cush is of the sons of Ham, and Midian is of the sons of Keturah, whom she bore to Abraham."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:37.548312861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}